    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Refine OpenMP directives to optimize work sharing, reductions, scheduling, and thread granularity for the sliding window technique in finding the maximum sum submatrix.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Added parallel region with dynamic scheduling for outer loop.\",\n    \"Used reduction clause for mxSum to ensure correct accumulation of maximum sum across threads.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <omp.h>\\n\\nint main() {\\n\\tint n,s;\\n\\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\\n\\tstd::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n\\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) \\n\\t\\t\\tscanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n\\tassert(s<n);\\n\\tassert(n<8000);\\n\\tassert(s>0);\\n\\tassert(n>0);\\n\\n\\tint sum = 0;\\n\\tfor(int i=0;i<s;i++)\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<s;j++)\\n\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\n\\tint mxSum = sum;\\n\\n\\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(dynamic)\\n\\tfor(int i=0; i<=n-s; i++) {\\n\\t\\tint local_sum = 0;\\n\\t\\tif(i==0) {\\n\\t\\t\\tlocal_sum = sum;\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) { \\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal_sum -= matrix[i-1][k];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal_sum += matrix[i+s-1][k];\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0; j<=n-s; j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\tif(j==0 && i!=0) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) { \\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal_sum -= matrix[k+i][j-1];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tlocal_sum += matrix[k+i][j+s-1];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, local_sum);\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tprintf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The parallel region is applied to the outer loop iterating over rows. The reduction clause ensures that the maximum sum (mxSum) is correctly updated across threads. Dynamic scheduling is used to balance the workload among threads.\"\n}"
